1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:06,337
If the Earth suddenly stopped moving
around the Sun, we would fall into it.

2
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:09,296
It would take about sixty-five days.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,198
Right now, Earth is racing along its
orbit at thirty kilometres every second.

4
00:00:20,198 --> 00:00:25,289
That sideways speed is the only
thing that keeps us from falling in.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,452
Nothing could actually stop a planet.

6
00:00:28,452 --> 00:00:34,453
This is a thought experiment. But suppose
that tonight, somehow, it simply stopped.

7
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,861
Day one. The Sun rises,
exactly as it always has.

8
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:43,874
We are already falling.

9
00:00:43,874 --> 00:00:49,758
By tonight we're moving at half a kilometre
per second, and no one can feel a thing.

10
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:51,595
Day ten.

11
00:00:51,595 --> 00:00:58,422
We've fallen two million kilometres. The
Sun is two percent wider. Nobody could tell.

12
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:04,377
Without an orbit, the seasons freeze.
Wherever it was summer, it stays summer.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,149
Day thirty. A whole month has gone by, and
we've covered only one seventh of the way.

14
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:15,306
But sunlight is already a third stronger.

15
00:01:15,306 --> 00:01:21,879
On a rough estimate, the world is heading toward
an average of nearly forty degrees Celsius.

16
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,438
Here's the cruel part.

17
00:01:25,438 --> 00:01:30,708
Gravity grows stronger the closer you
get, so the fall keeps speeding up.

18
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:34,529
The first half of the distance
takes fifty-three days.

19
00:01:34,529 --> 00:01:37,434
The second half takes less than twelve.

20
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,021
Day forty-two.

21
00:01:41,021 --> 00:01:47,066
We cross the orbit of Venus. Sunlight
is twice as strong as when we started.

22
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:52,752
Across most of the planet, simply
being outdoors would now be deadly.

23
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,598
Day fifty-seven. Mercury's orbit. It took
fifty-seven days to get here. From here to the Sun:

24
00:02:01,598 --> 00:02:03,091
one more week.

25
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,777
The Moon is still with us.

26
00:02:06,777 --> 00:02:14,657
In these last days, the Sun's pull begins to tear it
away from Earth. But it can't escape. It's falling too.

27
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:22,870
By the end of day sixty, sunlight is
twelve times stronger. Day sixty-two:

28
00:02:22,870 --> 00:02:26,925
twenty-five times. Day
sixty-three: nearly fifty.

29
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,998
Sixty-four days have passed.

30
00:02:32,998 --> 00:02:39,422
Thirteen hours remain. We're moving at a
hundred and fifty kilometres every second.

31
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:46,626
Eight hours left. The Sun is nearly
twenty times wider than it used to be.

32
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,968
Even now, the oceans haven't boiled away.

33
00:02:50,968 --> 00:02:59,939
They're too deep. All the sunlight Earth absorbs on the
entire fall could boil off only the top fifteen metres or so.

34
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:07,171
One hour left. The Sun is seventy
times wider than it used to be.

35
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,099
If anyone could still look,
they'd see its surface churning:

36
00:03:12,099 --> 00:03:16,561
cells of glowing plasma, each
about the size of a country.

37
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:24,315
In the final minutes, the Sun's tides
would begin to stretch the planet itself.

38
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:33,561
We arrive at more than six hundred kilometres per second,
almost exactly the speed you'd need to escape the Sun.

39
00:03:33,561 --> 00:03:38,451
At that speed, Earth crosses
its own width in twenty seconds.

40
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,028
And the Sun would barely notice.

41
00:03:45,028 --> 00:03:49,203
Earth is less than a
three-hundred-thousandth of its mass.

42
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,513
None of this will happen.
But here is the strange part:

43
00:03:54,513 --> 00:03:57,568
we are falling toward the Sun right now.

44
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:04,517
We always have been. An orbit is just a fall,
with enough sideways speed to keep missing.

45
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:12,450
For four and a half billion years, Earth has
been falling around the Sun, and missing.

